      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T21:19:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks different than the original logic.  It was just \"If I have HOGP, use pseudo address, otherwise use identity\"\n\nWhen allowSwitchingHidAndHogp goes live, this will all be removed, shouldn\u0027t it be the same as the old logic until then?",
      "revId": "f69f11c575792ec9deb34c0005d7d8cc6dd8c7fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a248b456_a42b4849",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hid/HidHostService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T21:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a change in logic when the flag is enabled.\n\nConsider a case where the remote device has both HID and HOGP and is using RPA in bondable mode. Pseudo address would an RPA.\nSince the remote device has HOGP profile, it will always use RPA which does not work with HID profile.",
      "parentUuid": "139a1ea4_31c79104",
      "revId": "f69f11c575792ec9deb34c0005d7d8cc6dd8c7fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54b4761d_3ae31a49",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hid/HidHostService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T21:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So to clarify, the native stack always expect pseudo address for HOGP, and public address / identity address for HID for dual mode devices paired via LE -\u003e Classic CTKD with RPA used on LE?",
      "parentUuid": "a248b456_a42b4849",
      "revId": "f69f11c575792ec9deb34c0005d7d8cc6dd8c7fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6428dc2_2791a37c",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hid/HidHostService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T22:17:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the remote device uses RPA for LE pairing, HID host cannot correctly determine if the BR/EDR ACL is connected or not. Specifically, `BTM_IsAclConnectionUp()` claims that the pseudo address is not connected over BR/EDR. I am not sure if it is true for when LE ACL status is requested for the identity address.\n\nOne way to fix this problem would have been to ensure that the whole native core stack is able to match both IA and pseudo addresses properly.\nI found that it was less risky to select the address to use in HidHostService since it already made the transport selection as well. Also there was a precedent for selecting address in HidHostService.",
      "parentUuid": "54b4761d_3ae31a49",
      "revId": "f69f11c575792ec9deb34c0005d7d8cc6dd8c7fe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
